$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.2.1. Synthesis of 2-(pentadeuteriophenyl)pyridine (d 5-1a)S11 To a
stirred solution of phenylboronic acid-d 5 (0.50 g, 3.94 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4
(0.088 g, 0.08 mmol) and Na2CO3 (2.25 g, 21.21 mmol) in toluene (12 ml),
water (12 mL), ethanol (2 mL), and 2-bromopyridine (0.479 mg, 3.03 mmol)
were added under nitrogen. The reaction mixture was refluxed for 14 h and
cooled to room temperature. To the reaction mixture was added aqueous
NH4Cl (15 mL), extracted with EtOAc three times, dried over MgSO4, and
then evaporated under reduced pressure to afford the crude product, which
was further purified by flash chromatography on silica gel with
n-hexane/EtOAc. 2-(pentaduteriophenyl)pyridine (0.35 g, 72%). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.67 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.67 - 7.65 (m, 2H), 7.25-6.96
(m, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 157.2, 149.5, 139.1, 136.5, 128.3 (t,
J = 24.0 Hz, 1CD) 128.1(t, J = 24.0 Hz, 2CD), 126.3(t, J = 24.0 Hz, 2CD),
121.9, 120.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
